 "files": [
  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# CRT Screen\n\nA scene behind curved tube glass: barrel distortion, an RGB phosphor mask, scanlines that bow with the picture, bloom around bright text and corners that run off into black. Runs its WebGL shader over its own built-in scene (a render queue list; title, rows and background from variables), not over the host video. The only motion is a 1 % brightness breath, so it holds as a look.\n\nCategory: filters. Length: 3 s. WebGL: yes.\n\nUse when:\n- Something should read as shown on a tube rather than rendered flat: retro terminals, arcade beats, an old dashboard being demoed.\n- The content is high contrast, bright text on a dark field, which the phosphor mask and bloom were built for.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The story is worn tape rather than a monitor: use vhs-filter.\n- It should read as photographed rather than displayed: use camera-lens.\n- The tube should switch off rather than run: use tv-power-off.\n- Content sits close to the frame edge: the barrel warp pushes the corners into the dark rim.\n\nVariables:\n- title (string): Title, default \"Render queue\"\n- items (string): Rows, default \"intro-scene.mp4 | Done; feature-tour.mp4 | Rendering; pricing-outro.mp4 | Queued\"\n- background (color): Background, default \"#101828\"\n- curvature (number, 0-2): Curvature, default 1\n- scanlines (number, 0-1.5): Scanlines, default 1\n- mask_scale (number, 1-6): Mask scale, default 2\n- vignette (number, 0-1.5): Vignette, default 1\n- resolution (number, 0.25-1): Resolution, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  CRT Screen\n\n  A scene behind curved glass: barrel distortion, an RGB phosphor mask, scanlines that bow with\n  the tube, bloom around bright text and a rim that falls away into black.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/crt-screen/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n\n  remocn captures its React children with the HTML-in-Canvas API, which a render machine does\n  not have. This block draws remocn's preview scene (a render queue, text from the variables) on a\n  2D canvas and runs remocn's fragment shader over it, so it applies the look to its own content,\n  not to the host video behind it.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"crt-screen\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"3\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    { \"id\": \"title\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Title\", \"description\": \"Small heading above the list.\", \"default\": \"Render queue\" },\n    { \"id\": \"items\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Rows\", \"description\": \"Rows of the list as name | status, separated by semicolons (up to 5).\", \"default\": \"intro-scene.mp4 | Done; feature-tour.mp4 | Rendering; pricing-outro.mp4 | Queued\" },\n    { \"id\": \"background\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Background\", \"description\": \"Background of the scene on the glass.\", \"default\": \"#101828\" },\n    { \"id\": \"curvature\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Curvature\", \"description\": \"How far the tube bulges. At 0 the frame stays flat and nothing is clipped at the corners.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 2, \"step\": 0.05 },\n    { \"id\": \"scanlines\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Scanlines\", \"description\": \"Strength of the horizontal lines, which bow with the picture.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 1.5, \"step\": 0.05 },\n    { \"id\": \"mask_scale\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Mask scale\", \"description\": \"Width of one phosphor stripe in frame pixels; a triad is three times this. Low reads as a fine grille, high as a coarse arcade tube.\", \"default\": 2, \"min\": 1, \"max\": 6, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\" },\n    { \"id\": \"vignette\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Vignette\", \"description\": \"How hard the picture falls off toward the rim.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 1.5, \"step\": 0.05 },\n    { \"id\": \"resolution\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"quality\", \"label\": \"Resolution\", \"description\": \"Share of the frame size the shader is drawn at, then scaled up. The phosphor mask needs 1; lower renders faster but softens it.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 1, \"step\": 0.05 }\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>CRT Screen</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link\n        rel=\"stylesheet\"\n        href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600&amp;family=Geist+Mono:wght@400&amp;display=block\"\n      />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          background: #000;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        .crt-stage {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n        }\n        .crt-canvas,\n        .crt-scene {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          width: 100%;\n          height: 100%;\n          display: block;\n        }\n        .crt-scene,\n        .crt-fallback {\n          display: none;\n        }\n        .crt-fallback {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n        }\n        .crt-scan {\n          background: repeating-linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.34) 0px, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.34) 1.5px, transparent 1.5px, transparent 3px);\n        }\n        .crt-vig {\n          background: radial-gradient(ellipse 82% 78% at 50% 50%, transparent 45%, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.72) 100%);\n        }\n        .crt-off .crt-canvas {\n          display: none;\n        }\n        .crt-off .crt-scene,\n        .crt-off .crt-fallback {\n          display: block;\n        }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"crt-screen\" data-duration=\"3\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"crt-clip\" class=\"crt-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"3\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <canvas id=\"crt-scene\" class=\"crt-scene\"></canvas>\n          <div id=\"crt-scan\" class=\"crt-fallback crt-scan\"></div>\n          <div id=\"crt-vig\" class=\"crt-fallback crt-vig\"></div>\n          <canvas id=\"crt-canvas\" class=\"crt-canvas\"></canvas>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var NAME = \"crt-screen\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var stage = document.getElementById(\"crt-clip\");\n            var canvas = document.getElementById(\"crt-canvas\");\n            var scene = document.getElementById(\"crt-scene\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value.trim() : fallback;\n            }\n            function hex(value, fallback) {\n              var m = /^#?([0-9a-f]{3}|[0-9a-f]{6})$/i.exec(String(value || \"\").trim());\n              if (!m) return fallback;\n              var h = m[1].length === 3 ? m[1].replace(/./g, \"$&$&\") : m[1];\n              return \"#\" + h.toLowerCase();\n            }\n\n            var title = str(vars.title, \"Render queue\");\n            var rows = str(vars.items, \"intro-scene.mp4 | Done; feature-tour.mp4 | Rendering; pricing-outro.mp4 | Queued\")\n              .split(\";\")\n              .map(function (row) { return row.split(\"|\").map(function (part) { return part.trim(); }); })\n              .filter(function (row) { return row[0]; })\n              .slice(0, 5);\n            var background = hex(vars.background, \"#101828\");\n            var curvature = num(vars.curvature, 1, 0, 2);\n            var scanlines = num(vars.scanlines, 1, 0, 1.5);\n            var maskScale = num(vars.mask_scale, 2, 1, 6);\n            var vignette = num(vars.vignette, 1, 0, 1.5);\n            var resolution = num(vars.resolution, 1, 0.25, 1);\n\n            // ---- The scene: remocn's preview (CanvasSceneB), laid out for 1280×720 and scaled to the frame.\n            var W = Math.max(2, root.clientWidth);\n            var H = Math.max(2, root.clientHeight);\n            var cw = Math.max(2, Math.round(W * resolution));\n            var ch = Math.max(2, Math.round(H * resolution));\n            scene.width = cw;\n            scene.height = ch;\n            var SANS = \"Geist, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif\";\n            var MONO = \"'Geist Mono', ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace\";\n            var INK = \"#f2f2f2\";\n            var MUTED = \"#8b8f9a\";\n            var TONES = [\"#a1eebd\", \"#ffb38e\", \"#d4b3ff\"];\n            function setFont(ctx, weight, size, family) {\n              ctx.font = weight + \" \" + size + \"px \" + family;\n            }\n            function fitFont(ctx, text, maxWidth, weight, size, family) {\n              setFont(ctx, weight, size, family);\n              var w = ctx.measureText(text).width;\n              if (w > maxWidth) {\n                size *= maxWidth / w;\n                setFont(ctx, weight, size, family);\n              }\n              return size;\n            }\n            function drawScene() {\n              var ctx = scene.getContext(\"2d\");\n              ctx.setTransform(cw / W, 0, 0, ch / H, 0, 0);\n              ctx.fillStyle = background;\n              ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);\n              var s = Math.min(W / 940, H / 720);\n              var pad = 96 * s;\n              var inner = W - pad * 2;\n              var titleH = 41 * s;\n              var rowH = 120 * s;\n              var line = Math.max(1, s);\n              var total = titleH + 34 * s + rows.length * (rowH + line);\n              var y = (H - total) / 2;\n              ctx.textBaseline = \"middle\";\n              ctx.textAlign = \"left\";\n              ctx.fillStyle = MUTED;\n              fitFont(ctx, title, inner, 400, 34 * s, SANS);\n              ctx.fillText(title, pad, y + titleH / 2);\n              y += titleH + 34 * s;\n              rows.forEach(function (row, i) {\n                ctx.fillStyle = \"#23304a\";\n                ctx.fillRect(pad, y, inner, line);\n                var mid = y + line + rowH / 2;\n                var label = row[1] || \"\";\n                var pillW = 0;\n                if (label) {\n                  var labelSize = fitFont(ctx, label, inner * 0.4, 500, 30 * s, SANS);\n                  pillW = ctx.measureText(label).width + 52 * s;\n                  var pillH = labelSize * 1.2 + 24 * s;\n                  var px = pad + inner - pillW;\n                  ctx.fillStyle = TONES[i % TONES.length];\n                  ctx.beginPath();\n                  ctx.roundRect(px, mid - pillH / 2, pillW, pillH, pillH / 2);\n                  ctx.fill();\n                  ctx.fillStyle = background;\n                  ctx.textAlign = \"center\";\n                  ctx.fillText(label, px + pillW / 2, mid);\n                  ctx.textAlign = \"left\";\n                }\n                ctx.fillStyle = INK;\n                fitFont(ctx, row[0], inner - pillW - 24 * s, 400, 44 * s, MONO);\n                ctx.fillText(row[0], pad, mid);\n                y += rowH + line;\n              });\n            }\n\n            // ---- remocn's shader (canvas-presentation vertex shader, crt-screen fragment shader).\n            var VERTEX = [\n              \"#version 300 es\",\n              \"in vec2 a_pos;\",\n              \"out vec2 v_uv;\",\n              \"void main() {\",\n              \"  v_uv = vec2(a_pos.x * 0.5 + 0.5, 0.5 - a_pos.y * 0.5);\",\n              \"  gl_Position = vec4(a_pos, 0.0, 1.0);\",\n              \"}\"\n            ].join(\"\\n\");\n            var FRAGMENT = [\n              \"#version 300 es\",\n              \"precision highp float;\",\n              \"uniform sampler2D u_scene;\",\n              \"uniform float u_frame;\",\n              \"uniform float u_curvature;\",\n              \"uniform float u_scanlines;\",\n              \"uniform float u_mask_scale;\",\n              \"uniform float u_vignette;\",\n              \"in vec2 v_uv;\",\n              \"out vec4 outColor;\",\n              \"const float PI = 3.141592653589793;\",\n              \"const float SCAN_LINES = 240.0;\",\n              \"vec2 warpTube(vec2 uv, float k) {\",\n              \"  vec2 p = uv * 2.0 - 1.0;\",\n              \"  float x2 = p.x * p.x;\",\n              \"  float y2 = p.y * p.y;\",\n              \"  p.x *= 1.0 + k * 0.11 * y2;\",\n              \"  p.y *= 1.0 + k * 0.17 * x2;\",\n              \"  p /= 1.0 + k * 0.045;\",\n              \"  return p * 0.5 + 0.5;\",\n              \"}\",\n              \"vec3 phosphorMask(float x, float scale) {\",\n              \"  float sub = mod(floor(x / max(scale, 1.0)), 3.0);\",\n              \"  vec3 lit = vec3(\",\n              \"    step(sub, 0.5),\",\n              \"    step(0.5, sub) * step(sub, 1.5),\",\n              \"    step(1.5, sub)\",\n              \"  );\",\n              \"  return mix(vec3(0.34), vec3(1.0), lit);\",\n              \"}\",\n              \"void main() {\",\n              \"  vec2 uv = warpTube(v_uv, u_curvature);\",\n              \"  vec2 edge =\",\n              \"    smoothstep(vec2(0.0), vec2(0.005), uv) *\",\n              \"    smoothstep(vec2(0.0), vec2(0.005), 1.0 - uv);\",\n              \"  float inside = edge.x * edge.y;\",\n              \"  vec4 base = texture(u_scene, uv);\",\n              \"  vec3 spread = vec3(0.0);\",\n              \"  for (int i = -2; i <= 2; i++) {\",\n              \"    spread += texture(u_scene, uv + vec2(float(i) * 0.0018, 0.0)).rgb;\",\n              \"  }\",\n              \"  spread /= 5.0;\",\n              \"  vec3 bloom = max(spread - 0.5, vec3(0.0));\",\n              \"  vec3 color = base.rgb;\",\n              \"  color *= phosphorMask(gl_FragCoord.x, u_mask_scale);\",\n              \"  color += bloom * 0.75;\",\n              \"  float scan = mix(1.0, 0.5 + 0.5 * cos(uv.y * SCAN_LINES * PI * 2.0), 0.55);\",\n              \"  color *= mix(1.0, scan, clamp(u_scanlines, 0.0, 1.5));\",\n              \"  vec2 vc = uv * 2.0 - 1.0;\",\n              \"  float radius = length(vc * vec2(0.86, 1.0));\",\n              \"  color *= mix(1.0, smoothstep(1.6, 0.35, radius), clamp(u_vignette, 0.0, 1.5));\",\n              \"  color *= 1.0 + 0.012 * sin(u_frame * PI / 30.0);\",\n              \"  color *= inside;\",\n              \"  outColor = vec4(clamp(color, 0.0, 1.0), max(base.a, 1.0 - inside));\",\n              \"}\"\n            ].join(\"\\n\");\n\n            canvas.width = cw;\n            canvas.height = ch;\n            var gl = canvas.getContext(\"webgl2\", { antialias: false, depth: false, stencil: false, preserveDrawingBuffer: true });\n            function compile(type, source) {\n              var shader = gl.createShader(type);\n              gl.shaderSource(shader, source);\n              gl.compileShader(shader);\n              if (!gl.getShaderParameter(shader, gl.COMPILE_STATUS)) throw new Error(gl.getShaderInfoLog(shader) || \"shader compile failed\");\n              return shader;\n            }\n            var paint = null;\n            var upload = function () {};\n            try {\n              if (!gl) throw new Error(\"WebGL2 is not available\");\n              var program = gl.createProgram();\n              gl.attachShader(program, compile(gl.VERTEX_SHADER, VERTEX));\n              gl.attachShader(program, compile(gl.FRAGMENT_SHADER, FRAGMENT));\n              gl.linkProgram(program);\n              if (!gl.getProgramParameter(program, gl.LINK_STATUS)) throw new Error(gl.getProgramInfoLog(program) || \"link failed\");\n              gl.useProgram(program);\n              var buffer = gl.createBuffer();\n              gl.bindBuffer(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, buffer);\n              gl.bufferData(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, new Float32Array([-1, -1, 1, -1, -1, 1, 1, 1]), gl.STATIC_DRAW);\n              var aPos = gl.getAttribLocation(program, \"a_pos\");\n              gl.enableVertexAttribArray(aPos);\n              gl.vertexAttribPointer(aPos, 2, gl.FLOAT, false, 0, 0);\n              var texture = gl.createTexture();\n              gl.activeTexture(gl.TEXTURE0);\n              gl.bindTexture(gl.TEXTURE_2D, texture);\n              gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_WRAP_S, gl.CLAMP_TO_EDGE);\n              gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_WRAP_T, gl.CLAMP_TO_EDGE);\n              gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_MIN_FILTER, gl.LINEAR);\n              gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_MAG_FILTER, gl.LINEAR);\n              gl.viewport(0, 0, cw, ch);\n              function u(name) { return gl.getUniformLocation(program, name); }\n              gl.uniform1i(u(\"u_scene\"), 0);\n              gl.uniform1f(u(\"u_curvature\"), curvature);\n              gl.uniform1f(u(\"u_scanlines\"), scanlines);\n              // the source measures the stripe in output pixels; the canvas is `resolution` × the frame.\n              gl.uniform1f(u(\"u_mask_scale\"), maskScale * resolution);\n              gl.uniform1f(u(\"u_vignette\"), vignette);\n              var frameLoc = u(\"u_frame\");\n              upload = function () {\n                gl.texImage2D(gl.TEXTURE_2D, 0, gl.RGBA, gl.RGBA, gl.UNSIGNED_BYTE, scene);\n              };\n              paint = function (frame) {\n                gl.uniform1f(frameLoc, frame);\n                gl.clearColor(0, 0, 0, 0);\n                gl.clear(gl.COLOR_BUFFER_BIT);\n                gl.drawArrays(gl.TRIANGLE_STRIP, 0, 4);\n              };\n            } catch (err) {\n              stage.classList.add(\"crt-off\");\n              if (window.console) console.warn(NAME + \":\", err.message);\n            }\n\n            // The scene is redrawn whenever a web font finishes loading, so no frame keeps a fallback face.\n            var fontEpoch = 0;\n            var sceneEpoch = -1;\n            var lastFrame = 0;\n            function render(frame) {\n              lastFrame = frame;\n              if (sceneEpoch !== fontEpoch) {\n                sceneEpoch = fontEpoch;\n                drawScene();\n                upload();\n              }\n              if (paint) paint(frame);\n            }\n            if (document.fonts && document.fonts.load) {\n              [\"400 34px Geist\", \"500 30px Geist\", \"400 44px 'Geist Mono'\"].forEach(function (face) {\n                document.fonts.load(face).then(function () { fontEpoch++; render(lastFrame); }, function () {});\n              });\n            }\n\n            var total = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"3\");\n            var totalFrames = Math.round(total * 30);\n            var clock = { frame: 0 };\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            tl.to(clock, {\n              frame: totalFrames,\n              duration: total,\n              ease: \"none\",\n              onUpdate: function () { render(Math.round(clock.frame)); }\n            }, 0);\n            render(0);\n            tl.seek(0);\n            window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n            window.__timelines[NAME] = tl;\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
